    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Aurora Innovation, Inc. is a self-driving freight company, according to its website, which describes its work as delivering the benefits of self-driving technology safely, quickly, and broadly. Its central product is the Aurora Driver, which the company describes as built with cutting-edge hardware and software backed by verifiable AI and as integrating autonomy into a customer's fleet. The site presents the technology through partner comments: a pilot program with Werner is described as autonomously hauling freight between Fort Worth and El Paso under a hybrid model combining Werner professional drivers with the Aurora Driver, and a Volvo comment states that the Aurora Driver is integrated into the Volvo VNL Autonomous. Another comment compares the system's intended performance to that of today's CDL drivers and cites millions of autonomous miles.\n\nThe company is a for-profit public company headquartered in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, trading under the ticker AUR, with CIK 0001828108.\n\nIts recorded litigation exposure is in Pennsylvania, where 154 matters are counted.",
